        "source_evidence": {
          "unit_id": "L0003",
          "start": 92,
          "end": 814,
          "quote": "**Justification:** FDISCO is specifically optimized to preserve fluorescence (including weak endogenous signals and synthetic dyes) for long-term storage (over 6 months) by using low-temperature dehydration and pH-adjusted solvents. For a 3 mm thick brain block, FDISCO provides excellent transparency and slight tissue hardening, which is ideal for repeated handling and imaging. To address the weak endogenous signal and the need for dendritic/local circuit analysis, a dual-target immunolabeling strategy is chosen: amplifying the sparse endogenous GFP with an Alexa Fluor secondary antibody, and co-labeling MAP2 with a different Alexa Fluor to visualize the detailed dendritic skeleton and local neuronal structures.\n",
